pluk's copy of the aephea macros

Copied from aephea 12-248 (../aephea-12-248/mac/aephea and mac/pud, the .zmm and .css
files; identical to the installed aephea at the time of copying). This copy is free to
diverge from aephea: changes for the pluk documentation are made here (plan/docstep1.txt).
Whatever proves itself may later go back to aephea.

The Makefile one level up puts this directory first in ZOEMSEARCHPATH, which zoem searches
before the installed aephea (checked in docstep1 item 1), so \import{pud/man.zmm} reads
mac/pud/man.zmm.

Changes from aephea 12-248:
  - aephea/base.zmm, aephea/base2.zmm: the roff font C (\fC) becomes CR (\f[CR]) in
    \v \m \tt and the verbatim environments; groff 1.23 warns 'cannot select font C'
    for the terminal devices (docstep1 item 2).
  - aephea/base.zmm, roff: a third special level for code, where - becomes \- (no line
    break after it; copies as ASCII hyphen-minus) and " stays "; \v \m \tt and the
    verbatim environments switch to it and back to level 1 (docstep1 item 3).
  - pud/man.zmm: the auxiliary files are per device, <base>.<device>.zmt and .zmr, since
    they contain device text; a key $source for field 4 of .TH (default '$name $tag');
    the HTML header no longer links to a .ps file (docstep1 item 3).
  - pud/man.zmm, HTML: HTML5 doctype, charset and viewport; a key $css_link (a linked
    stylesheet instead of the embedded base.css and $css_append, which remain the
    default); the header line has class docheader (docstep1 item 4).
  - aephea/base.zmm, HTML: \v \vq \m \tt write <code> instead of <tt>, which HTML5 no
    longer has (docstep1 item 4).
  - aephea/base.zmm, roff: the verbatim environment calls .ZR before and after the block,
    a hook defined empty in troff-defs (so pages that do not redefine it are unchanged);
    .ne counts two lines for it (docstep1 item 5).
  - A Markdown device, md (docstep1 item 6): md branches in aephea/base.zmm (inline
    fonts, links, specials with four levels, itemize, paragraphs, verbatim) and in
    pud/man.zmm (device check, header comment, \sec with an explicit anchor). It
    expects zoem -tl 2 (tools/runzoem.sh).
  - HTML structure (docstep1 item 8): itemize as <ul>/<li> (labels in span.itemlabel),
    verbatim as <pre class="verbatim">, paragraphs with classes instead of inline
    styles, ids instead of <a name>, <header> and <main> in pud/man.zmm, the table of
    contents as <nav class="toc"> (new key $tocnum); base.css follows the new markup.
  - pud/man.zmm, pages (docstep1 item 9): \sec records the output file of a section
    in the .zmr ({page}); links to sections (contents, \secref) go to page.html#id
    when on another page (pud::man::href); the HTML page opening and closing are the
    macros pud::man::htmlopen/htmlclose; the definitions and the .zmr loading in the
    environment's begin part run once per document, so that it can be begun again
    on a new output file. secref#1 for md.
  - Tables (docstep1 item 10): the table environment in aephea/base.zmm (\thead,
    \trow; keys spec, rowsep, roff) for html, roff (tbl, or a list) and md; pud/man.zmm
    key $preprocess, written as '\" <letters> on the first line of a man page; md
    escapes | in prose.
